{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It is the complement of the lexicographically greatest maximum independent set, not of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"least one: the least vertex of a symmetric difference is in one cover exactly when it is in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the other cover’s complement. That set is found as in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", with each choice the other way round: the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"core pass on a bipartite component leaves out each vertex it decides, a complete component","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keeps its greatest vertex, and any other component deletes a vertex whenever a maximum set","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"without it remains, with the reductions taking a simplicial vertex greater than all its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"neighbours. The cost is that of ","type":"text"},{"code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": O(m √n) on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bipartite components, and up to c exponential searches on a component of c vertices the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"tex